@H1 0. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
@P PURPOSE. Design a city any community can build, repair and extend, in which roads, paving, signage, water, drainage, waterways, electricity, internet, lighting, thermals, sound, agriculture, fauna, waste, ablutions, public facilities, transport, bridges, machinery and maintenance work as ONE synergetic system; stays safe under quake, storm, flood, fire and drought; and passes the Equidistributed Free Economy (EFE) filter on every decision.
@P METHOD. Receive > evaluate > study > absorb > conceptualise > ideate > evaluate > calculate > conclude > plan > exact > enhance > refine to plateau > generate. Every number here is computed by the accompanying scripted model (stdlib Python, unit-tested). Tables, schematics and the photo prompt are generated from one configuration file, so text, drawings and prompt agree by construction.
{{table:headline}}
@P CORE IDEA. The unit of the city is the AEQUCELL, a hexagon {{d.flat2flat|.0f}} m flat-to-flat. Cells meet along {{cfg.geometry.seam_width_m}} m AEQUSPINE seams: one shared corridor carrying the blue (swale, pond, flood route), green (forest verge, food forest), amber (power, storage, PV colonnade) and data (fibre, mesh, sensors) networks together with the slow streets and walks. Inside a cell, lanes and paths serve courts of about {{cfg.geometry.court_persons}} people. Every dwelling is a small power plant that feeds excess outward; every roof harvests water; every verge is a garden; every trench is shared and inspectable.
