@H2 1.2 EFE economics extracted (drives design constraints)
@P EQUALITY INVARIANT: Member_Value = Total_Treasury / Total_Members. Design translation: per-capita service levels (access, water, energy share, public space) are gated, so no member's entitlement depends on location. P95 walk to a daily node is {{res.access.cell_node.p95_min|.1f}} min, maximum {{res.access.cell_node.max_min|.1f}} min, node-distance Gini {{res.access.cell_node.gini|.2f}}.
@P ENTERPRISE CONTRIBUTION (0-5% bound) is the funding channel, PLEDGES fund capital, and the INTERNALIZATION PRIORITY ranks external costs so the largest dependency is internalised first. Section 9 computes external cost per member, the revenue per member needed to stay inside the 5% bound, and the ranking from this city's own flows.
@P EVER MODULE (50 ha, 500 residents; vertical agriculture 10 ha, residential 15, manufacturing + research 15, energy 5, commons 5) is the EFE precedent for a self-contained site. AEQUCELL generalises it into a tileable hexagon of {{res.land.pop_cell|,.0f}} residents on {{res.land.hex.area_ha|.1f}} ha. Vertical farming costs about {{res.food.mode_kwh_kg|.1f}} kWh per kg blended here (aeroponics 12 kWh/kg), so soil, tunnel and agri-PV carry the load and aeroponic towers stay a 5% niche.
@P PORTFOLIO BINDINGS (NextGen): AEQUBLOCK + AEQUBOND (earth walls, paving), FRAME CONSTRUCTIO (canopies, bridges), AEQUAQUA + AEQUAFLOW (house water, sanitation), AEQUIGROW + AEQUICROP + SALADIFRY (food), AEQUENERGY (community energy DAO), AEQUCHILL (cold chain), ALL-PURPOSE MANUFACTORY (fabrication node), AequMobi trikes + CARGO (mobility), MRCCS (freight, horizon T2), 3P-SRF fasteners, UNIVERSAL MAGNETIC CONNECT (charging). Personal-flight devices are NOT relied on; only landing reservations (T3).
@P PHYSICS GUARD. Machines described as generators are modelled as motor/generator CONVERTERS with efficiency below 1. Energy sources are sun, wind, biomass and partnership with the outer grid only (L-13).
@H2 1.3 AequCity v1.0 audit (the baseline)
{{table:v1_audit}}
@P RETAINED from v1.0: equidistribution as organising principle, civic commons at each node, three-horizon material logic, circular loops, local-first production, open documentation.
@H2 1.4 SA resource documents -> design inputs
@P SA Flora of Cleanse gives four Western Cape planting zones (fynbos garden, transition shrubland, succulent karoo garden, forest garden) and the rule to cultivate, never wild-harvest, threatened species: they map to wedge habitat strips, seam verges, court gardens and riparian ponds (6.6). The 12|12 NutriAir bioregional map supplies the Cape crop, fruit and herb palette; its pine and eucalyptus entries are excluded as regulated invasives and fire fuel. longevity sa.md is used only as an ingredient demand list (functional fungi, botanicals, proteins, minerals): the city provides growing capacity ({{res.food.mushroom_m2_city|,.0f}} m2 mushroom-house floor city-wide at {{cfg.food.mushroom_kg_pp}} kg per person per year). No efficacy claim is assessed.
